# W44-152: narrow the W44-151 W44-29 widen gate to d ∈ [3.0, 5.0]

date: 2026-05-21
sub-agent: w44-152 (loop session)
follow-on-to: W44-151 honest-stop (`ef35c5e1`)
chunk: 1 (SHIPPED — distance-narrowed admission)
status: SHIPPED — all hard acceptance gates PASS

## Mechanism

W44-151 introduced the `W44_151_HIGH_MASK_P25_MIN = 85.0` constant and
the `mask1x1_p25` plumbing through `compute_profile_for_search` (the
W44-29 outer dispatch helper) + `encode_inner` (inline copy), but
HONEST-STOPPED on the admission branch because the broad `d >= 3.0`
gate over-fired the default `high_d_photo_smooth_suppressed()` table on
1418519 d=6 (+4.3-4.6% bytes for only +0.07-0.28 SSIM2, dragging the
d=5/d=6 mean SSIM2 below the +1.0 acceptance bar).

The W44-151 honest-stop memo (and the W44-151 bench TSV `1418519` rows)
documented that the d=4 cluster was a clean win (-3% bytes + +0.55
SSIM2 mean) and the d=5 cluster was strong at e8+ (+1.13 SSIM2). The
ONLY drag was the d=6 cluster.

W44-152 ships the admission with a closed distance band:

```text
let w44_152_distance_in_band =
       self.distance >= W44_152_W44_151_MIN_DISTANCE   // 3.0
    && self.distance <= W44_152_W44_151_MAX_DISTANCE;  // 5.0
let w44_152_disable_env = std::env::var("JXL_W44_152_DISABLE") == "1"
                       || std::env::var("JXL_W44_151_DISABLE") == "1";
let w44_152_admit = !w44_152_disable_env
    && w44_152_distance_in_band
    && mask1x1_p25.is_some_and(|p25| p25 >= W44_151_HIGH_MASK_P25_MIN);
w44_29_gate || w44_91_gate || w44_152_admit
```

This is wired symmetrically into BOTH `compute_profile_for_search`
(the still-image helper used by the animation `bitstream.rs` path) AND
the inline copy inside `encode_inner` (the primary still-image dispatch
site). Both sites use identical predicates and identical env-hook
fallback.

## Cells

Same 72 cells as W44-151 (the bench is the SAME cell list; only the
production gate predicate and env-var name change):

* TARGET   = 1418519 d=4/5/6 × e7/e8/e9 (9 cells)
* PROTECT  = 1025469 d=2..6 × e7/e8/e9 (15 cells; mask_p25=60.64,
             must stay BYTE-IDENTICAL)
* SPOT     = {1189261, 1420710, 1531677, 7552578} × {e7/e8/e9} ×
             {d=3..6} (48 cells; all mask_p25 < 85, must stay
             BYTE-IDENTICAL)

Total: 72 cells × 2 modes (A = JXL_W44_152_DISABLE=1 baseline,
B = default = W44-152 active).

