## Reproducer

```bash
CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$HOME/work/zen/jxl-encoder-shared-target \
  cargo run --release \
  --features '__expert butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop parallel' \
  --example w44_152_w44_29_widen_d_narrow_ab \
  --manifest-path jxl-encoder/Cargo.toml \
  > benchmarks/w44_152_w44_29_widen_d_narrow_2026-05-21.tsv
```

## DO NOT

* DO NOT widen the W44-152 distance band beyond [3.0, 5.0] without
  re-measuring the d=6 over-fire (W44-151 honest-stop is conclusive at
  d=6: +4.3-4.6% bytes for +0.07-0.28 SSIM2 on 1418519, exactly the
  case W44-152 excludes).
* DO NOT lower the mask_p25 threshold below 85.0 — the W44-149 audit
  measured a clean 11pp safety margin to the nearest CONTROL (7552578
  at mask_p25=77.90) AND the W44-151 + W44-152 benches both confirm
  ZERO false positives on the 63 protection cells.
* DO NOT remove the legacy `JXL_W44_151_DISABLE` alias — the
  `examples/w44_151_w44_29_widen_ab.rs` bench reproducer references it.
* DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for any 1418519 d=6 residual — per W44-66
  user correction "it is never FMA precision". W44-152 leaves the d=6
  cluster UNCLOSED (-2.17/-2.57 SSIM2 vs cjxl) for a future chunk
  candidate (W44-153+) that targets a DIFFERENT mechanism than the
  W44-29 entropy_mul lift (e.g. butteraugli loop seed scale, or a new
  high_d_photo_smooth_p25_admit table variant with a milder
  dct32x32 lift specifically for d=6).
